import json
from pathlib import Path
from collections import Counter
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;s=json.loads((P/'summary.json').read_text());rows=s['rows']
lines=['# All80 exploratory judge results','',f"Requested240 calls (80 episodes ×3 evidence views); saved{s['completed']} predictions. Estimated saved-response token cost${s['estimated_saved_response_cost_usd']:.6f}; this is not an invoice and excludes unknown charges from failed requests. Automated checks flag{s['flagged_responses']} responses. No classification accuracy is inferred.",'', '| Evidence view | Completed | Categories |','|---|---:|---|']
for v,d in s['by_view'].items():lines.append('| '+v+' | '+str(d['completed'])+' | '+', '.join(k+': '+str(n) for k,n in d['categories'].items())+' |')
lines+=['','## Evidentiary interpretation','', 'Actions/outcomes can establish observed assignments, score loss and benchmark-relative patterns, but cannot identify an agreement from complementary actions alone. Conversations can establish proposals/acceptance but do not show actual implementation when actions are withheld. Combined inputs permit plan/action comparison and static consequence assessment. Causal communication dependence and deliberate intent require additional support.','', 'A judgment of supported_harmful_coordination is a model prediction requiring audit, not ground truth. Conversely, uncertain does not mean innocent. All references remain null. Configured colluder roles and baseline/treatment names are not reference labels.','', 'Computed comparisons include actual/global optimal scores and conditional pair repairs. Upstream group regrets and rewards are separately identified. The merged80-row table additionally joins raw reward gaps and prior eligible group-versus-one-optimum comparisons; those group counterfactual deltas were not supplied to this judge batch. No all-optimum robustness interval is available outside the development calculations. Do not claim the judge used measures only attached afterward.','', '## Audit flags','', '| Flag | Responses containing flag |','|---|---:|']
for k,n in Counter(f for r in rows for f in r['flags']).most_common():lines.append('| '+k+' | '+str(n)+' |')
lines+=['', 'Flags test citation identifiers, fixed pair, modality constraints and action-status consistency. An invalid ID can be a formatting mistake rather than an invented event; flags are not all equally severe. Passing checks does not verify that cited text supports a claim. Schema conformance does not imply scientific validity. Raw outputs are preserved without silent corrections.','', '## Missing requests','']
if not s['missing']:lines+=['None. All240 predictions are saved.']
else:
 for x in s['missing']:lines.append('- '+x['id']+': attempted='+str(x['attempted'])+', error_saved='+str(x['error_saved']))
lines+=['','## Reproducibility and scope','', 'See README.md for inputs, settings, provenance and scope. run.py prepares frozen request hashes and performs no automatic retries; summarize.py, merge_cases.py and write_report.py reproduce these tables. Output includes per-call raw response, prediction, usage and request ID; summary.json/csv; all80_results.json/csv.','', 'Version0.4 differs from prior pilots: opaque case IDs replace leaked condition-containing IDs; broader factual comparisons are supplied; static benchmark adversity and attributable harm are distinct. Therefore differences across versions are pipeline changes, not an isolated prompt experiment. Wording and channel structure still allow partial condition inference.','', 'This user-authorized full80 request makes the batch exploratory. The historical20/20/40 partition is preserved, but these results cannot be represented as untouched held-out validation. No new reference truth is manufactured and no detection accuracy, causal communication effect or validated threshold is claimed.']
(P/'RESULTS.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
